      "message": "**Double Endian-Swapping (`ft_scsi.cc`)** In `ReceiveAndValidateCsw`, you perform the following check:\n\n```c\n  if (ToLittleEndian(csw.signature) !\u003d kUsbMsCswSignature ||\n      ToLittleEndian(csw.tag) !\u003d ToLittleEndian(cbw.tag)) {\n\n```\n\nWhile this functions correctly, it relies on a double-negative logic quirk. The `cbw.tag` was *already* converted to Little-Endian when the `BulkCbWrap` was constructed. By calling `ToLittleEndian(cbw.tag)` here, you are inadvertently swapping it *back* to native endianness on Big-Endian systems. `ToLittleEndian(csw.tag)` swaps the wire Little-Endian to native, meaning both sides end up comparing the native values.\n\n* **Remedy:** Since both `cbw.tag` and `csw.tag` are in wire (Little-Endian) format, compare them directly: `if (csw.tag !\u003d cbw.tag)`.  \n* **Readability Tip:** Introduce a symmetric `FromLittleEndian` alias in `ft_util.h` (e.g., `constexpr T FromLittleEndian(T value) { return ToLittleEndian(value); }`). Reading *from* the wire should logically use `FromLittleEndian(csw.signature)`.",
