      "message": "**Silent Ignorance of Short USB Reads (`ft_scsi.cc`)** In `ReceiveBulkDataIn`, you properly request data from the USB device, but you do not verify if the device actually returned the expected number of bytes.\n\n```c\n  if (!data_buffer.empty()) {\n    auto recv_res \u003d device.Recv(data_buffer, timeout_ms);\n    if (!recv_res) { // Checks for transport error, but not short reads!\n      FT_LOGE(\"Data IN transfer failed.\");\n      return std::unexpected(recv_res.error());\n    }\n  }\n\n```\n\nIf the USB device responds with a short packet (e.g., 5 bytes instead of the requested 512), `recv_res` will evaluate to true (containing `5`). The function will then successfully return, leaving the rest of the caller\u0027s buffer uninitialized or holding stale data.\n\n* **Remedy:** Enforce a strict length check against the buffer size, or update the function to return the actual number of bytes read so callers can react accordingly. Furthermore, you should evaluate the `csw.data_residue` field in `ReceiveAndValidateCsw` to detect mismatched transfer sizes at the SCSI level.",
