      "message": "You have two identical implementations of the SHA-256 hashing logic: `CalculateSha256` in `updater.cc` and `ComputeSha256` in `test_utils.h`.\n\n**The Fix:** Centralize this in `updater.h` so both production and test code use the exact same function.\n\n**In `util/focaltech/updater.h`**, add the include and declaration:\n\n```c\n#include \u003copenssl/sha.h\u003e\n\n// ... inside focaltech namespace ...\nstd::array\u003cuint8_t, SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH\u003e ComputeSha256(\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e data);\n\n```\n\n*   **In `util/focaltech/updater.cc`**, expose the implementation and remove the old static one:\n    ```cpp\n    std::array\u003cuint8_t, SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH\u003e ComputeSha256(\n        std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e data) {\n      std::array\u003cuint8_t, SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH\u003e hash{};\n      SHA256(data.data(), data.size(), hash.data());\n      return hash;\n    }\n    ```\n\n\n*(Don\u0027t forget to update the call inside `VerifyData` to use `ComputeSha256`!)*\n\n\n* **In `util/focaltech/test_utils.h`**, completely delete `ComputeSha256` and just `#include \"updater.h\"`.",
